    "done_when": "Correct the false cold-compile claim of the kernel landing. Finding (independent review of cfs-kernel-compile-cost, 2026-10-06): tests/biot/test_kernel_compile_cost.py's _compile disables jax_enable_compilation_cache only after point and geometry setup has initialised cache use, and jax.clear_caches does not reset that state in the installed JAX, so h200-fresh-cold.log records two jit_jet cache hits with stored compile costs 86 and 81 seconds while the fragment and the ledger claim 11.2 and 7.9 seconds as cold. Done when: (1) the cold-compile test measures each arm in a fresh subprocess whose environment disables the persistent compilation cache before jax is imported (the cache directory unset and the enable flag off in the subprocess environment), asserts from the cache guard rows that the measured program was a miss, and refuses to report a wall as cold when it was a hit; (2) that measurement is re-run on the H200 in one job for the base-revision kernels (loaded through importlib from git show at the kernel landing's recorded base, orientation_base_sha of run r-20261005T223546294421) and for the landed kernels, recording both true cold walls and executable bytes; (3) the under-30-second assertion passes on the true figure or becomes pytest.mark.xfail(strict=True) naming the measured wall, never a loosened bound; (4) docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/cfs-kernel-compile-cost.html gets an appended correction paragraph with an id attribute, placed after the landing paragraph and never editing the earlier sentences, stating the earlier figures were cache hits, the stored compile costs the log recorded, and the true cold walls now measured; reckon audit-doc reports 0 errors. Negative control: the corrected test, run once with the cache deliberately left enabled from a warmed directory, reports the hit and refuses to call the wall cold, with its log named in the manifest. Gates run on the H200 through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path under the run directory named in the manifest) --wait -- tests/biot/test_kernel_compile_cost.py -vv -s, never on the login node; on a compute node uv is not invoked and the shared environment's interpreter runs directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run's worktree (orientation_worktree in the manifest); every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync; configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies; the manifest's commits line lists every commit.",
